LUXDATE ANDROID UI MAP
Version: current code scan
Source app: LuxApp
Platform focus: Android
Purpose: current-state screen inventory, content map, and navigation flow for UI planning

==================================================
1. ROOT APP FLOW
==================================================

1. App shell
- `App.jsx` mounts `AppNavigator` inside gesture + safe-area providers.
- If user is not authenticated: auth stack is shown.
- If authenticated but profile has no `name`: onboarding screen is forced.
- If authenticated and onboarded: main app stack is shown.
- Incoming calls can interrupt and open `IncomingCall` globally.

2. Top-level navigator structure
- Auth stack:
  - `Login`
  - `Otp`
  - `Onboard`
- Main app tabs:
  - `ForYou`
  - `Chat`
  - `Me`
- Extra stack screens above tabs:
  - `GirlProfile`
  - `Conversation`
  - `CallHistory`
  - `IncomingCall`
  - `OutgoingCall`
  - `VideoCall`
  - `Wallet`
  - `CoinPack`
  - `VIPPlans`
  - `TransactionHistory`

3. First-run / entry flow
- App launch
- If logged out -> `Login`
- `Login` success -> `Otp`
- `Otp` success:
  - if backend/store returns a user with `name`, app proceeds into main app
  - if user has no `name`, app shows `Onboard`
- `Onboard` success -> main app stack -> `MainTabs` -> usually lands in `ForYou`

4. Main app tab flow
- `ForYou` tab is the discovery/home surface
- `Chat` tab is inbox
- `Me` tab is profile/account

5. Important navigation gaps found
- `ForYouScreen` tries to open `SearchScreen`, but `SearchScreen` is not registered in `AppNavigator`.
- There is no separate dedicated "Welcome" screen route. The current `Login` screen acts as both welcome and login entry.

==================================================
2. GLOBAL VISUAL LANGUAGE
==================================================

1. Overall look
- Dark UI throughout.
- Neon/cyber-luxury style.
- Strong use of magenta, cyan, violet, gold accents.
- Rounded corners everywhere.
- Most screens use black or near-black backgrounds.
- Several auth screens use a soft mesh glow background.

2. Core recurring UI patterns
- Rounded icon buttons with dark tertiary backgrounds.
- High-contrast headers with bold text.
- Magenta primary CTA buttons.
- Cyan secondary emphasis in some auth and wallet areas.
- Modals and sheets for filters, coins, gifts, payment gateways, and confirmations.

3. Tone of copy
- Mixed tone:
  - Auth screens use stylized cyber-luxury copy.
  - Main app uses more direct product copy.
  - Some screens still contain placeholder or rough copy.

==================================================
3. SCREEN-BY-SCREEN DETAILS
==================================================

--------------------------------------------------
SCREEN: LOGIN
Route: `Login`
Role: welcome + phone entry
--------------------------------------------------

Current look
- Full-screen dark background with two large soft neon mesh glows.
- Centered layout.
- Square logo card with `LX`.
- Large glowing `LuxDate` title.
- Small uppercase subtitle.
- Single phone-input row with `+91` prefix.
- Large glowing magenta CTA button.

Visible content
- Logo text: `LX`
- App title: `LuxDate`
- Subtitle: `Enter the neon grid.`
- Phone placeholder: `000 000 0000`
- CTA loading state: `TRANSMITTING...`
- CTA normal state: `INITIALIZE LINK`
- Footer/legal text:
  - `BY CONTINUING, YOU AGREE TO OUR TERMS OF SERVICE AND PRIVACY PROTOCOLS.`
- Error box shows auth/store error text when present.

What the page does
- User enters 10-digit phone number.
- On CTA tap, app sends OTP.
- If success, navigates to `Otp` with the phone number in params.

Flow
- Comes from: app launch when logged out
- Goes to: `Otp`

Notes
- This is effectively your current welcome screen.
- There is no standalone marketing intro before it.

--------------------------------------------------
SCREEN: OTP
Route: `Otp`
Role: OTP verification
--------------------------------------------------

Current look
- Same mesh neon background family as login.
- Centered title and subtitle.
- Six single-character OTP boxes in one row with a visual middle gap.
- Cyan-themed confirmation button.

Visible content
- Title: `SECURITY CHECK`
- Subtitle: `Enter transmission code sent to +91 {phone}`
- CTA loading state: `VERIFYING...`
- CTA normal state: `CONFIRM ACCESS`
- Error box shows auth/store error text when present.

What the page does
- User enters 6-digit OTP.
- On verify, store handles auth state.
- Navigation after success is indirect through auth state:
  - onboarded user -> main app
  - non-onboarded user -> `Onboard`

Flow
- Comes from: `Login`
- Goes to:
  - `Onboard` if profile incomplete
  - main app if profile already complete

--------------------------------------------------
SCREEN: ONBOARD
Route: `Onboard`
Role: profile completion
--------------------------------------------------

Current look
- Full-screen dark background with mesh glow.
- Simple centered form.
- Much less flashy than login/OTP.
- Plain text heading with glass-style inputs and gender chips.

Visible content
- Title: `Welcome to LuxDate`
- Subtitle: `Curated matching for the elite.`
- Field label: `Your Name`
- Name placeholder: `e.g. Alexander`
- Field label: `Age`
- Age placeholder: `Must be 18+`
- Field label: `I identify as`
- Gender options:
  - `Male`
  - `Female`
  - `Other`
- CTA loading state: `Creating Profile...`
- CTA normal state: `Enter the Club`

What the page does
- Collects name, age, gender.
- Submit calls onboarding store action.
- After success, auth/onboarding state pushes user into the main app.

Flow
- Comes from:
  - `Otp` for new/incomplete user
  - forced onboarding path for authenticated user without `name`
- Goes to: main app tabs

Notes
- This is the only profile-completion screen currently.
- No photo, preferences, interests, location, or profile preview in this flow.

